 "status": "active",
 "title": "C1: generic foreign organic (C-H excess over the collagen line, or an organic film)",
 "description": "excess = (r1728 + r1762 + r2262 + r2350) - (a + b x (r1510 + r2044 + r2175)), r = mean E (evidence kernel) over centre +- 2 nm. Fires if excess > the cut. Full variant only: film = mean E over peak_nm +- half_width_nm minus mean E over trough_nm +- half_width_nm (the 2298/2325 organic-film contrast); C1 also fires if film >= its cut (record: film, film_fired; null where the film rule does not run). Runs only when no plaster, wax or ester sign fired and C1 passes its B6b gate; when the long-wave tail is unreliable for C1 (check.longwave) the truncated variant runs. When C1 is gated and check.acquisition lists a fallback, the swir1 variant (1728 + 1762 over 1510 nm only, no film rule, no soft line) runs instead. Adds a flag; blocks an evidence lift. soft_tier: the soft line of the 'possible thin coating' note (check.signs soft_tier), full and truncated.",
 "licence": "CC-BY-4.0",
 "created": "2026-10-03",
 "provenance": {
  "basis": "Phase 0a A5: (a, b) least squares on 1,201 clean bone scans (public reference bones and unreleased archaeological fauna; statistics only); cut = 99.5th percentile of the specimen-grouped out-of-fold excess (8.00), rounded. False alarms 6/1,201 (0.50%) out of fold; held out across sources 0.30-0.80%.",
  "film": "DECISIONS 100-103 (2026-10-05): the 2298/2325 contrast separates C-H-combination-heavy coatings from bone (report 11 section 11.5). Cut 17.8 = the 99.5th percentile of 2,322 clean standard-res scans (8 sets; pre-registered rule: <= 1% pooled, <= 2% per set): 0.5% pooled, worst set 1.6%. Adds 14 of 715 coated scans the shipped signs miss, mostly Butvar (museum 30% -> 53%), for 0.4% extra clean false alarms. Not in the truncated variant (the > 2300 nm region is too noisy then).",
  "swir1": "2026-10-13 (pre-registered; planning hires_fallback): (a, b) least squares on the 1,201 clean scans; cut 10.8 = 1.1 x the largest clean value seen in the high-resolution study sets (out-of-fold 99.5th percentile 7.2 gave 5% false alarms on one dark set). 0 of 2,322 clean standard-resolution scans (8 sets) exceed it. On real coated standard-resolution scans it catches far less than the full signs (film rule included): alkyd 34% vs 85%, glued fauna 22% vs 88%, PVAc 3% vs 65%, museum Butvar 0% vs 47%: a reduced check for heavy consolidants, used only where the full C1 cannot run."
 },
